course: dictionary
lesson: 4370
title: Gym: a place, a room, a lesson
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A gym is a big room or building for sport and exercise, with equipment like weights and bars. «Gym» is short for gymnasium. Read the words around it to check: «Most people also went to the public baths every day, like a swimming pool, gym and café all in one.» Here a gym is a place where people go to exercise.
explain: Sometimes gym means the school hall, used for sport and games. Gym class is the school lesson for sport and exercise, also called PE. The clues show this: «one day in PE he went dizzy, fainted and cut his chin on the gym floor.» PE and the gym floor tell you the gym is a room at school.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. If «a big room for sport» still makes sense, you have it right. If the sentence stops making sense, look again at the clues around the word.
fact: Gym is a noun. Its plural is gyms.
fact: «Gym» is short for gymnasium.
fact: A gym can be a room or building, the school hall, or a lesson called gym class.
fact: Exercise in the gym helps keep your heart and muscles strong.
fact: The y in «gym» does the job of a vowel, like the y in «myth» and «sky».
exercise: What is a gym? | A type of cake | A kind of sweet drink | *A big room or building for sport and exercise
exercise: Gym class is the school lesson for sport and exercise. What is another name for it? | Maths | *PE | Art
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that means a place for sport: «Most people also went to the public baths every day, like a swimming pool, gym and café all in one.» | every | people | *gym | café
test: In «one day in PE he went dizzy, fainted and cut his chin on the gym floor», where did Ben fall? | At home | *In the gym | A swimming pool
test: What part of speech is gym? | Adjective | *Noun | Verb
exam: In «Ben cut his chin on the gym floor», what does gym mean? | *A big room for sport and exercise | A shop that sells food | A bag for books | A type of bird
